[NONE]: State LOW disabled
[MACCREADY]: State High if gross vario is greater than MacCready setting.
[AVERAGE]: State HIGH if gross vario value is greater than average gross vario value.␀␀␀␀ToneCruiseLiftDetectionType␀Cruise lift trigger␀Comparison method used to detect cruise states for switching to lift tones during cruise.
[NONE]: LIFT tone disabled in cruise
[RELATIVE ZERO] LIFT tone when relative vario greater than zero.
[GROSS ZERO] LIFT tone when glider is climbing.
[RELATIVE MC/2] LIFT tone when relative vario greater than half MC.
[NET MC/2] LIFT tone when airmass velocity greater than half MC.␀␀␀␀ToneAveragerVarioTimeScale␀␀Climb averager scale␀␀␀␀Time scale used for vario averager.␀ToneAveragerCruiseTimeScale␀Cruise averager scale␀␀␀Time scale used for cruise speed command averager.␀␀ToneMeanVolumeCircling␀␀Circling volume␀Mean volume level in circling modes.␀␀␀␀%d/8␀␀␀␀ToneMeanVolumeCruise␀␀␀␀Cruise volume␀␀␀Mean volume level in cruise modes. If set to zero, scales with airspeed.␀␀␀␀ToneBaseFrequencyOffset␀Base frequency␀␀Adjustment to base frequency of tones in all modes.␀VarioTimeConstantCircling␀␀␀Filter circling␀Variometer low pass filter time constant in circling mode.␀␀VarioTimeConstantCruise␀Filter cruise␀␀␀Variometer low pass filter time constant in cruise mode.␀␀␀␀TonePitchScale␀␀Tone pitch scale␀␀␀␀Adjustment to base pitch scale of tones in all modes.␀␀␀ 1.0s␀␀␀ 1.3s␀␀␀ 1.8s␀␀␀ 2.7s␀␀␀ 0.0s␀␀␀ 0.8s␀␀␀ 1.7s␀␀␀ 3.5s␀␀␀ 7.5s␀␀␀15.0s␀␀␀30.0s␀␀␀Relative>0␀␀Relative>MacCready/2␀␀␀␀Gross>0␀Net>MacCready/2␀Relative>MacCready␀␀Net>MacCready␀␀␀Gross>MacCready␀Gross>Average␀␀␀TotalEnergyMixingRatio␀␀TE mixing␀␀␀Proportion of TE probe value used in total energy mixing with pitot/static total energy.␀␀␀␀CalibrationAirSpeed␀ASI cal.␀␀␀␀Calibration factor applied to measured airspeed to obtain indicated airspeed.␀␀␀CalibrationTEStatic␀TE static cal.␀␀Calibration factor applied to static pressure used in total energy calculation.␀CalibrationTEDynamic␀␀␀␀TE dynamic cal.␀Calibration factor applied to dynamic pressure used in total energy calculation.␀␀␀␀HasPressureTE␀␀␀TE port␀Whether the Total Energy port is connected.␀HasPressurePitot␀␀␀␀Pitot port␀␀Whether the Pitot port is connected.␀␀␀␀HasPressureStatic␀␀␀Static port␀Whether the Static port is connected.␀␀␀HasPressureStall␀␀␀␀Stall port␀␀Whether the Stall pressure port is connected.␀␀␀HasAccelerometer␀␀␀␀Accelerometer␀␀␀Whether the internal accelerometer is used. Only change this if the accelerometer has malfunctioned or the instrument cannot be installed with correct alignment.␀␀␀HasTemperature␀␀Whether a temperature and humidity sensor is installed. Set to 0 to disable, 255 to enable auto-detect; otherwise the 1-Wire device ID can be specified.␀␀␀␀BaudrateA␀␀␀Baud rate Vega␀␀Baud rate of serial device connected to Vega port X1. Use this when using a third party GPS or data-logger instead of FLARM. If FLARM is connected the baud rate will be fixed at 38400. For OzFLARM, the value can be set to 19200.␀␀␀␀FlarmConnected␀␀FLARM connected␀Enable detection of FLARM. Disable only if FLARM is not used or disconnected.␀␀␀EnablePDASupply␀PDA power␀␀␀Enable output of the +5 V power supply for a PDA or similar device at Vega connector X2. If Vega is connected to Altair, set this to Off.␀␀␀TE vario␀␀␀␀This produces a fake TE vario gross vertical velocity. It can be used when in circling mode to demonstrate the lift tones. When not in circling mode, set this to a realistic negative value so speed command tones are produced.␀␀␀This produces a fake airspeed. It can be used when not in circling mode to demonstrate the speed command tones.␀This forces the variometer into circling or cruise mode␀PDVSC,S,DemoMode,0␀␀PDVSC,S,DemoMode,3␀␀Vario Demo␀␀PDVDD,{},{}␀VegaDemo: failed to format payload: {}␀␀VegaDemo: failed to format payload␀␀Airbrake locked␀Flaps␀␀␀Gear down␀␀␀Acknowledge␀Speed command␀␀␀Vario circling␀␀Locked␀␀Not locked␀␀Up␀␀Middle␀␀Down␀␀␀␀Positive␀␀␀␀Neutral␀Negative␀␀␀␀FLARM range setup␀␀␀BAUD1␀␀␀BAUD2␀␀␀BAUD␀␀␀␀THRE␀␀␀␀ACFT␀␀␀␀LOGINT␀␀PRIV␀␀␀␀NOTRACK␀Baud rate port 1␀␀␀␀Baud rate port 2␀␀␀␀Threshold␀␀␀Select a speed threshold.␀␀␀Automatic␀␀␀%u m/s␀␀Stealth mode␀␀␀␀No tracking mode␀␀␀␀Range setup␀Hang glider␀Paraglider␀␀Flying saucer␀␀␀Unmanned aerial vehicle␀Static object␀␀␀PCASRANGE␀␀␀PCASVRANGE␀␀ADSBRANGE␀␀␀ADSBVRANGE␀␀Range␀␀␀PCAS range␀␀PCAS vertical range␀ADSB range␀␀ADSB vertical range␀FLARM range␀Reset␀␀␀FLARM range estimate␀␀␀␀%s â€“ %s␀␀␀%u / %u␀Unlimited␀␀␀The FLARM did not send its range statistics.␀␀␀␀Antenna␀The FLARM keeps the statistics for each of its two radio channels.␀␀Data points␀Below minimum range␀Measured sectors of this channel whose mean range is shorter than FLARM's minimum: 2 nm ahead, 1 nm to the sides and behind.  Check the antenna installation.␀␀␀Range setting␀␀␀The FLARM reports no aircraft beyond this distance.  The plot shows it as a dashed circle when it is within the plotted range.␀␀Reset the range statistics? Do this after a change to the antennas; the FLARM then collects them anew.␀␀The FLARM did not confirm the reset.␀␀␀␀Contacts with other FLARM aircraft in flight, counted once in every sector they passed, with the largest distance they were received at there.  The sector shows the mean of the larger half of these distances, the line across it the largest one.␀␀␀␀Measured sectors whose estimated range is shorter than FLARM's minimum: 2 nm ahead, 1 nm to the sides and behind.  Check the antenna installation.␀␀Reset the range estimate? Do this after a change to the antenna; XCSoar then collects it anew.␀␀Per-class filter settings. For airspaces where both
type (CTR, FIR, ...) and class are given, the type
takes precedence over class in XCSoar.
Columns:
  Show  - draw airspaces of this class on the map
  Warn  - enable warnings when approaching / inside
  Clrnc - allow granting a clearance to suppress
           warnings from other overlapping airspaces␀␀Clrnc␀␀␀Airspace Renderer Settings␀␀Change Border Color␀Change Fill Color␀␀␀Border Width␀␀␀␀The width of the border drawn around each airspace. Set this value to zero to hide the border.␀␀Fill Mode␀␀␀Defines how the airspace is filled with the configured color.␀␀␀Filled␀␀Only padding␀␀␀␀Not filled␀␀Wind Settings␀␀␀Dump␀␀␀␀Ballast dump time is 0 in plane profile.
Open Plane configuration now?␀␀Flight Setup␀␀␀␀xcsoar://config/planes␀␀Crew␀␀␀␀All masses loaded to the glider beyond the empty weight including pilot and copilot, but not water ballast.␀Ballast␀Ballast of the glider. Press "Dump/Stop" to toggle count-down of the ballast volume according to the dump rate specified in the configuration settings.␀%.0f l␀␀Wing loading␀␀␀␀The current wing loading, calculated from the glider's empty weight, crew weight, and ballast. Shown in red when the glider is heavier than its MTOW.␀␀␀How clean the glider is. Set to 0% for clean, larger numbers as the wings pick up bugs or get wet. 50% indicates the glider's sink rate is doubled.␀%.0f %%␀Area pressure for barometric altimeter calibration. This is set automatically if Vega is connected.␀Max. temp.␀␀The day's maximum ground temperature. A dry adiabat from it against the outside air temperature measured while climbing gives the estimated thermal ceiling; the cloud base needs a humidity probe as well. Both are drawn on the temperature trace page of the Analysis dialog, once the glider has climbed through the layer.␀Configuration␀␀␀Expert␀␀Add␀Turn off␀␀␀␀Restart␀Map Display␀Glide Computer␀␀Gauges␀␀Look␀␀␀␀Services␀␀␀␀Audio␀␀␀Language, Input␀RASP␀␀␀␀Scoring␀Task Rules␀␀Turnpoint Types␀Elements␀␀␀␀Orientation␀Overlays␀␀␀␀UserLevel␀␀␀This target has NoTrack enabled and may not be persisted.␀␀␀Do you want to set this FLARM contact as your new teammate?␀New Teammate␀␀␀␀Team␀␀␀␀Traffic Details␀ (%d dBm)␀␀␀Callsign␀␀␀␀Change callsign␀Airport␀Radio frequency␀Plane type␀␀Data source␀Traffic source␀␀Own code␀␀␀␀Mate code␀␀␀Rel. bearing␀␀␀␀Flarm Lock␀␀Unknown Competition Number␀␀Set new teammate␀␀␀␀Set code␀␀␀␀Set WP␀␀Team Code␀␀␀Distance to go␀␀Task Calc␀␀␀Barograph␀␀␀Settings␀␀␀␀Climb␀␀␀Thermal Band␀␀␀␀Vario Histogram␀Wind at Altitude␀␀␀␀Set Wind␀␀␀␀Glide Polar␀%s: %s (%s %d kg)␀␀␀MacCready Speeds␀␀␀␀Temperature Trace␀␀␀Task Speed␀␀Calc␀␀␀␀Information␀Download the example checklist or create your