Visit us at:
[https://xcsoar.org](https://xcsoar.org)␀␀␀␀About␀␀␀Authors␀News␀␀␀␀Quick Menu  %d/%d␀␀␀Quick Menu␀␀RemoteStick␀Master Volume␀␀␀The overall audio output volume.␀␀␀␀MasterAudioVolume␀␀␀IDR_WAV_AIRSPACE_INSIDE␀IDR_WAV_AIRSPACE_NEAR␀␀␀IDR_WAV_AIRSPACE_ABOVE␀␀Failed to acknowledge airspace warning␀␀Failed to acknowledge airspace warning for day␀␀Inside␀␀%s  ␀␀␀␀Ack Day␀Revoke␀␀Maximum start speed exceeded␀␀␀␀%s (%s > %s)␀␀␀␀In sector, arm advance when ready␀␀␀Dismiss␀Add this turn point?␀␀␀␀USR,%02u%02u%02u,%s,%06X␀␀␀␀DISMISS␀MUTE␀␀␀␀Mute 1 min␀␀climbing␀␀␀␀%u o'clock␀␀Direction unknown␀␀␀Traffic urgent␀␀close in␀␀␀␀, %s %u s␀␀␀Jet␀Drone␀␀␀There is nothing interesting near this location.␀␀␀␀Map elements at this location␀␀␀Vario and thermal␀␀␀Glide␀␀␀Speed and attitude␀␀Wind and weather␀␀␀␀Airspace and team␀␀␀Other␀␀␀InfoBox caption (gravity/load factor)␀␀␀Altitude GPS␀␀␀␀Alt GPS␀Altitude above mean sea level reported by the GPS. (Touch-screen/PC only) In simulation mode, this value is adjustable with the up/down arrow keys; the right/left arrow keys cause the glider to turn.␀Height AGL␀␀H AGL␀␀␀Navigation altitude minus the terrain elevation obtained from the terrain file. The value is coloured red when the glider is below the terrain safety clearance height.␀Thermal climb, last 30 s␀␀␀␀TC 30s␀␀30-second rolling average climb rate based on reported GPS altitude, or vario if available. The number in smaller font reflects the climb rate for the current thermal since circling started.␀␀Next bearing␀␀␀␀True bearing of the next waypoint. For AAT tasks, this is the true bearing to the target within the AAT sector.␀GR instantaneous␀␀␀␀GR Inst␀Instantaneous glide ratio over ground, given by the ground speed divided by the vertical speed (GPS speed) over the last 20 seconds. Negative values indicate climbing cruise. If the vertical speed is close to zero, the displayed value is '---'.␀␀␀␀GR cruise␀␀␀GR Cruise␀␀␀Distance from the top of the last thermal, divided by the altitude lost since the top of the last thermal. Negative values indicate climbing cruise (height gain since leaving the last thermal). If the vertical speed is close to zero, the displayed value is '---'.␀Speed ground␀␀␀␀V GND␀␀␀Ground speed measured by the GPS. The small value shows the head or tail wind difference to TAS for the current vector. If this InfoBox is active in simulation mode, pressing the up and down arrows adjusts the speed, and left and right turn the glider.␀␀␀␀Last thermal average␀␀␀␀TL Avg␀␀Total altitude gain/loss in the last thermal divided by the time spent circling. The seconds in smaller font reflect the time spent circling.␀␀␀Last thermal gain␀␀␀TL Gain␀Total altitude gain/loss in the last thermal. The number in smaller font reflects the overall climb rate for the last thermal.␀␀Last thermal duration␀␀␀TL duration␀Time spent circling in the last thermal. The number in smaller font reflects the overall climb rate for the last thermal.␀␀␀MacCready setting␀␀␀Current MacCready setting and mode (manual or auto). The comment shows the MacCready speed-to-fly. At MacCready 0, with a task or Goto active, that speed is adjusted for wind toward the waypoint and need not match the polar's still-air best glide. With MacCready above 0, wind is not used. (Touch-screen/PC only) When this InfoBox is active, use the up/down cursor keys to adjust the MacCready setting.␀␀Next distance␀␀␀WP Dist␀Distance to the currently selected waypoint. For AAT tasks, this is the distance to the target within the AAT sector.␀␀␀Next altitude difference␀␀␀␀WP AltD␀Arrival altitude at the next waypoint relative to the safety arrival height. For AAT tasks, the target within the AAT sector is used.␀␀␀Next altitude required␀␀WP AltR␀Additional altitude required to reach the next turn point. For AAT tasks, the target within the AAT sector is used.␀Next waypoint␀␀␀Next WP␀Name of the currently selected turn point. When this InfoBox is active, using the up/down cursor keys selects the next/previous waypoint in the task. (Touch-screen/PC only) Pressing the enter cursor key brings up the Airfields/waypoint details.␀␀␀␀Final altitude difference␀␀␀Fin AltD␀␀␀␀Arrival altitude at the final task turn point relative to the safety arrival height.␀␀␀␀Final altitude required␀Fin AltR␀␀␀␀Additional altitude required to finish the task.␀␀␀␀Speed task average␀␀V Task Avg␀␀Average cross-country speed while on current task, not compensated for altitude.␀␀␀␀Final distance␀␀Fin Dist␀␀␀␀Distance to finish around remaining turn points.␀␀␀␀Final GR (TE) deprecated␀␀␀␀Deprecated, there is no TE compensation on GR, you should switch to the "Final GR" info box.␀␀␀␀Terrain elevation␀␀␀Terr Elev␀␀␀Elevation of the terrain above mean sea level, obtained from the terrain file at the current GPS location.␀␀Thermal average␀TC Avg␀␀Altitude gained/lost in the current thermal, divided by time spent thermalling.␀Thermal gain␀␀␀␀TC Gain␀Altitude gained/lost in the current thermal.␀␀␀␀Magnetic track reported by the GPS. (Touch-screen/PC only) If this InfoBox is active in simulation mode, pressing the up/down arrows adjusts the track.␀Instantaneous vertical speed, as reported by the GPS, or the intelligent vario total energy vario value if connected to one.␀␀␀␀Wind speed␀␀Wind speed estimated by XCSoar. Manual adjustment is possible with the connected InfoBox dialogue. Pressing the up/down cursor keys to cycle through settings, adjust the values with left/right cursor keys.␀␀␀Wind bearing␀␀␀␀Wind bearing estimated by XCSoar. Manual adjustment is possible with the connected InfoBox dialogue. Pressing the up/down cursor keys to cycle through settings, adjust the values with left/right cursor keys.␀AAT time␀␀␀␀AAT Time␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task time remaining. Goes red when time remaining has expired.␀␀␀␀AAT max. distance ␀␀AAT Dmax␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task maximum distance possible for remainder of task.␀AAT min. distance␀␀␀AAT Dmin␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task minimum distance possible for remainder of task.␀AAT speed max. distance␀AAT Vmax␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task average speed achievable if flying maximum possible distance remaining in minimum AAT time.␀␀AAT speed min. distance␀AAT Vmin␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task average speed achievable if flying minimum possible distance remaining in minimum AAT time.␀␀Airspeed IAS␀␀␀␀V IAS␀␀␀Indicated Airspeed reported by a supported external intelligent vario.␀␀Barometric altitude␀Alt Baro␀␀␀␀Barometric altitude obtained from a device equipped with a pressure sensor.␀Speed MacCready␀V MC␀␀␀␀MacCready speed-to-fly for optimal flight to the next waypoint. In cruise flight mode, this speed-to-fly is calculated for maintaining altitude. In final glide mode, this speed-to-fly is calculated for descent. At MacCready 0, with a task or Goto active, this speed is adjusted for wind toward the waypoint and need not match the polar's still-air best glide. With MacCready above 0, wind is not used.␀␀␀Percentage climb␀␀␀␀% Climb␀Percentage of time spent in climb mode. These statistics are reset upon starting the task.␀␀Flight duration␀Flt Duration␀␀␀␀Time elapsed since takeoff was detected.␀␀␀␀G load␀␀Magnitude of G loading reported by a supported external intelligent vario. This value is negative for pitch-down manoeuvres.␀␀␀␀Next GR␀WP GR␀␀␀Required glide ratio over ground to reach the next waypoint, given by the distance to the next waypoint divided by the height required to arrive at the safety arrival height.␀␀Time local␀␀Time loc␀␀␀␀GPS time expressed in local time zone.␀␀Time UTC␀␀␀␀GPS time expressed in UTC.␀␀Task time to go␀Fin ETE␀Estimated time required to complete task, assuming performance of ideal MacCready cruise/climb cycle.␀␀␀Next time to go␀WP ETE␀␀Estimated time required to reach next waypoint, assuming performance of ideal MacCready cruise/climb cycle.␀Speed dolphin␀␀␀Vopt␀␀␀␀Instantaneous MacCready speed-to-fly, making use of netto vario calculations to determine dolphin cruise speed on the glider's current track. In cruise flight mode, this speed-to-fly is calculated for maintaining altitude. In final glide mode, this speed-to-fly is calculated for descent. In climb mode, this switches to the speed for minimum sink at the current load factor (if an accelerometer is connected). When Block mode speed-to-fly is selected, this InfoBox displays the MacCready speed. At MacCready 0, with a task or Goto active, this speed is adjusted for wind toward the waypoint and need not match the polar's still-air best glide. With MacCready above 0, wind is not used.␀␀Netto vario␀Instantaneous vertical speed of air-mass, equal to vario value less the glider's estimated sink rate. Best used if airspeed, accelerometers and vario are connected, otherwise calculations are based on GPS measurements and wind estimates.␀␀␀Task arrival time␀␀␀Fin ETA␀Estimated arrival local time at task completion, assuming performance of ideal MacCready cruise/climb cycle.␀␀␀␀Next arrival time␀␀␀WP ETA␀␀Estimated arrival local time at next waypoint, assuming performance of ideal MacCready cruise/climb cycle.␀␀Bearing difference␀␀Brng D␀␀Difference between the glider's track (direction of motion across the ground) and the bearing to the next waypoint, or for AAT tasks, the bearing to the target within the AAT sector. GPS navigation is based on the track, and the track may differ from the glider's heading when there is wind. Chevrons point to the direction the glider needs to alter course to correct the bearing difference, that is, to make it so that the glider is tracking directly toward the next waypoint. This calculation accounts for the curvature of the Earth.␀Outside air temperature␀OAT␀Outside air temperature measured by a probe if supported by a connected intelligent variometer.␀Rel Hum␀Relative humidity of the air in percent as measured by a probe if supported by a connected intelligent variometer.␀␀Forecast temperature␀␀␀␀Max Temp␀␀␀␀Forecast temperature of the ground at the home airfield, used in estimating convection height and cloud base in conjunction with outside air temperature and relative humidity probe. (Touch-screen/PC only) Pressing the up/down cursor keys adjusts this forecast temperature.␀␀␀␀AAT distance around target␀␀AAT Dtgt␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task distance around target points for remainder of task.␀AAT speed around target␀AAT Vtgt␀␀␀␀Assigned Area Task average speed achievable around target points remaining in minimum AAT time.␀L/D vario␀␀␀L/D Vario␀␀␀Instantaneous lift/drag ratio, given by the indicated airspeed divided by the total energy vertical speed, when connected to an intelligent variometer. Negative values indicate climbing cruise. If the total energy vario speed is close to zero, the displayed value is '---'.␀␀␀Airspeed TAS␀␀␀␀V TAS␀␀␀True Airspeed reported by a supported external intelligent vario. The value is blue when estimated from ground speed and wind.␀␀Team code␀␀␀Current Team code for this aircraft. Use this to report to other team members. The last team aircraft code entered is displayed underneath.␀Team bearing␀␀␀␀Team Brng␀␀␀Bearing to the team aircraft location at the last team code report.␀Team bearing difference␀Team BrngD␀␀Relative bearing to the team aircraft location at the last reported team code.␀␀Team range␀␀Team Dist␀␀␀Range to the team aircraft location at the last reported team code.␀Speed task instantaneous␀␀␀␀V Task Inst␀Instantaneous cross-country speed while on current task, compensated for altitude. Equivalent to instantaneous Pirker cross-country speed.␀␀Distance home␀␀␀Home Dist␀␀␀Distance to home waypoint (if defined).␀Speed task achieved␀V Task Ach␀␀Achieved cross-country speed while on current task, compensated for altitude. Equivalent to Pirker cross-country speed remaining.␀␀␀AAT delta time␀␀AAT dT␀␀Difference between estimated task time and AAT minimum time. Coloured red if negative (expected arrival too early), or blue if in sector and can turn now with estimated arrival time greater than AAT time plus 5 minutes.␀Thermal average over all␀␀␀␀T Avg␀␀␀Time-average climb rate in all thermals.␀␀␀␀Task req. total height trend␀␀␀␀RH Trend␀␀␀␀Trend (or neg. of the variation) of the total required height to complete the task.␀Battery percent␀Percentage of device battery remaining (where applicable) and status/voltage of external power supply.␀␀Final GR␀␀␀␀Fin GR␀␀Required glide ratio over ground to finish the task, given by the distance to go divided by the height required to arrive at the safety arrival height.␀Alternate 1␀Altn 1␀␀Name and bearing to the best alternate landing location.␀␀␀␀Alternate 2␀Altn 2␀␀Name and bearing to the second-best alternate landing location.␀Alternate 1 GR␀␀Altn 1 GR␀␀␀Geometric gradient to the arrival height above the best alternate landing location. This is not adjusted for total energy.␀␀Height above take-off␀␀␀H T/O␀␀␀Height based on an automatic take-off reference elevation (like a QFE reference).␀␀␀GR average␀␀GR Avg␀␀Distance flown during the configured averaging period divided by the altitude lost during that period. Negative values are shown as ^^^ and indicate climbing cruise (height gain). For GR >200, the value is shown as +++. You can configure the averaging period in the system setup (suggested: 60, 90 or 120s). Lower values will be closer to GR Inst, and higher values will be closer to GR Cruise. Note: The distance is not the straight line between your previous and current positions; it is the actual path distance flown (including zigzags). This value is not calculated while circling.␀␀Experimental 1␀␀Exp1␀␀␀␀Contest distance␀␀␀␀Cont Dist␀␀␀Instantaneous evaluation of the flown distance according to the configured Contest rule set.␀␀␀␀Experimental 2␀␀Exp2␀␀␀␀CPU load␀␀␀␀CPU␀CPU load consumed by XCSoar averaged over 5 seconds.␀␀␀␀Next altitude arrival␀␀␀WP AltA␀Absolute arrival altitude at the next waypoint in final glide. For AAT tasks, the target within the AAT sector is used.␀Free RAM␀␀␀␀Free RAM as reported by OS.␀Flight level␀␀␀␀Pressure Altitude given as Flight Level. If barometric altitude is not available, FL is calculated from GPS altitude, given that the correct QNH is set. In case the FL is calculated from the GPS altitude, the FL label is coloured red.␀␀Barogram␀␀␀␀Trace of altitude during flight.␀␀␀␀Vario trace␀Vario Trace␀Trace of vertical speed, as reported by the GPS, or the intelligent vario total energy vario value if connected to one.␀Netto vario trace␀␀␀Netto Trace␀Trace of vertical speed of air-mass, equal to vario value less the glider's estimated sink rate.␀␀␀␀Thermal climb trace␀TC Trace␀␀␀␀Trace of average climb rate each turn in circling, based of the reported GPS altitude, or vario if available.␀␀␀Climb band␀␀Climb Band␀␀Graph of average circling climb rate (horizontal axis) as a function of altitude (vertical axis).␀␀␀Task progress␀␀␀Progress␀␀␀␀Clock-like display of distance remaining along task, showing achieved task points.␀␀Time under max. start height␀␀␀␀Start Height␀␀␀␀Contiguous period during which the aircraft has been below the task start maximum height.␀␀␀Task time to go (ground speed)␀␀Fin ETE VMG␀Estimated time required to complete task, assuming current ground speed is maintained.␀␀Next time to go (ground speed)␀␀WP ETE VMG␀␀Estimated time required to reach next waypoint, assuming current ground speed is maintained.␀␀␀␀Attitude indicator␀␀Attitude indicator (artificial horizon) display calculated from flight path, supplemented with acceleration and variometer data if available.␀␀␀Nearest airspace horizontal␀Near AS H␀␀␀Horizontal distance to the nearest airspace.␀␀␀␀Nearest airspace vertical␀␀␀Near AS V␀␀␀Vertical distance to the nearest airspace. A positive value means the airspace is above you; a negative value means the airspace is below you.␀␀Next MC0 altitude difference␀␀␀␀WP MC0 AltD␀Arrival altitude at the next waypoint with MC 0 setting relative to the safety arrival height. For AAT tasks, the target within the AAT sector is used.␀Wind, head component␀␀␀␀Head Wind␀␀␀Current head wind component. Head wind is calculated from TAS and GPS ground speed if airspeed is available from an external device; otherwise, the estimated wind is used.␀Terrain collision␀␀␀Terr Coll␀␀␀Distance to the next terrain collision along the current task leg. At this location, the altitude will be below the configured terrain clearance altitude.␀␀Altitude (Auto)␀Alt Auto␀␀␀␀Barometric altitude obtained from a device equipped with a pressure sensor, or GPS altitude if barometric altitude is not available.␀␀␀␀Thermal next leg equivalent␀T Next Leg␀␀Main value: thermal climb rate on the next leg that is equivalent to a thermal climb rate equal to the MacCready setting on the current leg. Secondary value: thermal climb rate on the current leg that is equivalent to a thermal climb rate equal to the MacCready setting on the next leg.␀␀Wind, head component (simplified)␀␀␀Head Wind *␀Current head wind component. The simplified head wind is calculated by subtracting GPS ground speed from TAS if airspeed is available from an external device.␀␀Task cruise efficiency␀␀Cruise Eff␀␀Efficiency of cruise. 100 indicates perfect MacCready performance. This value estimates your cruise efficiency according to the current flight history with the set MC value. Calculation begins after task is started.␀Thermal␀Circular thermal assistant that shows the lift distribution over each part of the circle.␀␀␀Start open/close countdown␀␀Start open␀␀Signed countdown until the start gate opens or closes (now). Value colour and secondary line reflect gate state at the current time: Waiting (blue), Open (green), Closed (red). PEV window overrides task gate when set.␀␀␀Start open/close countdown at reaching␀␀Start reach␀Same gate as Start open. Main value is estimated time to reach the start line (MacCready leg when available, else distance / ground speed). Value colour and secondary line reflect gate state at that ETA: Too early (blue), Can start (green), Too late (red).␀␀␀␀Next radial␀True bearing from the next waypoint to your position.␀␀␀ATC radial␀␀Bearing from the selected reference location to your position. The distance is displayed in nautical miles for communication with ATC. If declination is entered, magnetic bearing is given to match VOR radials.␀␀␀Speed task last hour␀␀␀␀V Task H␀␀␀␀Average cross-country speed while on current task over the last hour, not compensated for altitude.␀Next distance (nominal)␀WP Dist-N␀␀␀Distance to the currently selected waypoint. For AAT tasks, this is the distance to the origin of the AAT sector.␀␀␀Circle diameter␀Circle D␀␀␀␀Circle diameter. Displays estimated circle diameter and full circle flight time. Useful for evaluating best thermalling mode with a glider at different wing loading.␀␀␀Distance takeoff␀␀␀␀Takeoff Dist␀␀␀␀Distance to where take-off was detected.␀␀␀␀Contest speed␀␀␀Cont Speed␀␀Instantaneous evaluation of the flown speed according to the configured contest rule set.␀␀␀Final MC0 altitude difference␀␀␀Fin MC0 AltD␀␀␀␀Arrival altitude at the final waypoint with MC 0 setting relative to the safety arrival height.␀Next arrow␀␀Arrow pointing to the currently selected waypoint. The name of the waypoint and the distance are also shown. The position used is the optimized position of the active waypoint in the current task, the center of a selected goto waypoint or the target within the AAT sector for AAT tasks.␀␀Next waypoint arrival time (ground speed)␀␀␀WP ETA VMG␀␀Estimated arrival time at next waypoint, assuming current ground speed is maintained.␀␀␀Percentage non-circling climb␀␀␀% Str Climb␀Percentage of time spent climbing without circling. These statistics are reset upon starting the task.␀␀Percentage climb chart␀␀Climb %␀Pie chart of time circling and climbing, circling and descending, and climbing non-circling.␀␀␀␀Number of used satellites␀␀␀Satellites␀␀Number of satellites currently used by the GPS module. If this information is unavailable, the displayed value is '---'.␀␀␀␀Active Radio Frequency␀␀Active radio frequency.␀Standby Radio Frequency␀Standby radio frequency.␀␀␀␀Thermal time␀␀␀␀TC Time␀Time spent in the current thermal.␀␀Alternate 2 GR␀␀Altn 2 GR␀␀␀Geometric gradient to the arrival height above the second-best alternate landing location. This is not adjusted for total energy.␀␀␀Heart␀␀␀Heart rate in beats per minute.␀Transponder Code␀␀␀␀XPDR Code␀␀␀Currently set transponder code.␀Engine CHT␀␀CHT␀Engine cylinder head temperature.␀␀␀Engine EGT␀␀EGT␀Engine exhaust gas temperature.␀Engine Revolutions Per Minute␀␀␀RPM␀Engine revolutions per minute.␀␀AAT dT and task ETA␀AATdeltaOrETA␀␀␀For AAT tasks: AAT delta time and estimated time of arrival; for racing tasks: estimated time of arrival.␀␀␀Speed task estimated␀␀␀␀V Task Est␀␀Estimated average cross-country speed for current task as of task completion, assuming performance of ideal MacCready cruise/climb cycle.␀␀␀Home altitude difference␀␀␀␀Home AltD␀␀␀Arrival altitude at the home waypoint relative to the safety arrival height.␀␀␀␀Speed task leg␀␀V Task Leg␀␀Average cross-country speed while on current task leg, not compensated for altitude.␀␀␀␀Alternate 1 altitude difference␀Altn 1 AltD␀Arrival altitude at the best alternate landing location using Safety MC, relative to the safety arrival height.␀Alternate 2 altitude difference␀Altn 2 AltD␀Arrival altitude at the second-best alternate landing location using Safety MC, relative to the safety arrival height.␀␀Home waypoint name, arrival altitude difference relative to the safety arrival height, and distance. Click to change the home waypoint.␀Altitude IGC␀␀␀␀Logger pressure altitude when the device provides it (igc_pressure_altitude), otherwise ISA pressure altitude only (1013.25 hPa; not QNH-corrected). Does not show barometric AMSL or GPS height â€” use other InfoBoxes for navigation.␀␀␀␀Current QNH pressure setting used for barometric altitude calculation. The line below shows that altitude when a pressure sensor is available. Tap the infobox to open the setup panel and adjust QNH manually.␀Active Waypoint␀Active WP␀␀␀Active waypoint: shows the next task waypoint when an ordered task is loaded, otherwise the Goto waypoint. Displays the waypoint name, arrival altitude difference relative to the safety arrival height, and distance. Click to choose a different waypoint (a task waypoint to skip to that leg, or any waypoint to set as Goto when no task is loaded).␀␀Previous Waypoint␀␀␀Prev WP␀Previous waypoint: when an ordered task is loaded, automatically tracks the task waypoint before the active leg (the start waypoint when on the first leg). Displays the waypoint name, arrival altitude difference relative to the safety arrival height, and distance. Click to choose a different waypoint to display (task waypoints when a task is loaded, otherwise the full waypoint list); selection is informational only and never advances the task or sets a Goto. With a task loaded, choose "Resume auto tracking" at the top of the list to revert to automatic tracking.␀␀␀␀SpO2␀␀␀␀Blood oxygen saturation in percent, from a Bluetooth pulse oximeter.␀␀␀␀Water ballast on board, in litres. The comment shows the wing loading, in red when the glider is heavier than its MTOW. The value is blue while ballast is being dumped. Tap to change the ballast.␀Speed VMG␀␀␀V VMG␀␀␀The component of the ground speed in the direction of the next waypoint. It equals the ground speed when tracking straight at it, falls to zero at right angles and goes negative when flying away. It puts a number on what a detour off the direct course costs.␀␀Fixed text␀␀Title, value and comment entered by the pilot. Tap to edit.␀MAN␀AUTO␀␀␀␀Altn {} {}␀␀Altn {} {} {}␀␀␀+++␀no QNH␀␀Not flying␀␀{:03}␀␀␀{}ft␀␀␀␀^^^␀{:3.0f}␀{}:1␀␀␀␀MC AUTO␀MC MANUAL␀␀␀{:2.2f}␀No GPS␀␀BLOCK␀␀␀DOLPHIN␀Waiting␀Open␀␀␀␀Closed␀␀Time Below␀␀95% ␀␀␀␀{}{:d}:{:02}␀␀␀␀Start unknown␀␀␀Too early␀␀␀Can start␀␀␀Too late␀␀␀␀{}.{:03} {}␀{:02}:{:02}␀{:02}␀␀␀Resume auto tracking␀␀␀␀Reference␀␀␀{:.1f} pts␀␀???␀no wind␀{:2.1f}␀{:2.0f}␀7500␀␀␀␀7600␀␀␀␀7700␀␀␀␀{} %␀␀␀␀Cruise␀␀FinalGlide␀␀%+.0f␀␀␀Area pressure for barometric altimeter calibration.  This is set automatically if Vega connected.␀␀␀Ground elevation for device calibration (meters).␀␀␀Brg␀%s %c%s␀Spd␀Mag declination␀Magnetic declination used to calculate radial to reference. Negative values are W declination, positive is E.␀␀␀%.0f kHz␀␀␀␀{:X}␀␀␀␀Firmware expired␀␀␀␀Firmware update error␀␀␀Voltage Low␀UI error␀␀␀␀Audio error␀ADC error␀␀␀SDCARD error␀␀␀␀LED error␀␀␀EEPROM error␀␀␀␀GPIO error␀␀General hardware error␀␀Transponder receiver Mode-C/S/ADS-B unserviceable␀␀␀GPS communication␀␀␀Configuration of GPS module␀GPS antenna␀RF communication␀␀␀␀Another FLARM device with the same radio ID is being received␀␀␀Wrong ICAO 24-bit address or radio ID␀␀␀Communication␀␀␀Flash memory␀␀␀␀Pressure sensor␀Obstacle database expired␀␀␀Flight recorder␀Engine-noise recording not possible␀Invalid obstacle database license␀␀␀Invalid IGC feature license␀Invalid AUD feature license␀Invalid ENL feature license␀Invalid RFB feature license␀Invalid TIS feature license␀Generic error␀␀␀Flash File System error␀Failure updating firmware of external display␀␀␀Device is operated outside the designated region. The device does not work.␀Range analyzer␀␀No error␀␀␀␀Reduced functionality␀␀␀Fatal problem␀␀␀IDR_WAV_TRAFFIC_URGENT␀␀IDR_WAV_TRAFFIC_IMPORTANT␀␀␀IDR_WAV_TRAFFIC_LOW␀IDR_WAV_LEVEL␀␀␀IDR_WAV_ABOVE␀␀␀IDR_WAV_BELOW␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_1␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_2␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_3␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_4␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_5␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_6␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_7␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_8␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_9␀␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_10␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_11␀␀␀IDR_WAV_OCLOCK_12␀␀␀Expect early task arrival␀␀␀Expect arrival past sunset␀␀Significant wind change␀CLR,%02u%02u%02u␀␀␀␀OWN,%02u%02u%02u,%.0f,%.1f,%.1f,%.1f␀␀␀␀TGT,%02u%02u%02u,%06X,%u,%.0f,%.0f,%.0f,%.0f,%.1f,%.1f,%.1f,%s,␀,%.1f␀␀␀Logger I/O error␀␀␀␀%f %f␀␀␀jp2_box_get() failed␀␀␀␀Wrong JP magic␀␀